A||N||3||DaveL||87 2.5 a/c compressor||||1||
Z||000000||DaveL||08-07-2000||04:23 PM||||My compressor is finally taking a serious dump, making a hell of a lot of noise, and occasionally seizing up. My question is this, I can buy remanufactured units done by Four Seasons for $169.00, OR A NEW ac/dELCO UNIT FOR $309. Is it really woth going with the AC unit? Just had a new dryer put on it, and vacumed the system and changed it over to R134. Should I put in another accumulator with it when I do? The system didn't work for over two years, and has about 80,000 miles on it. Worked fine for a few weeks, but started getting warm again, then making horrible noise. One night with the headlights and the a/c on, the alternator light came on for a minute, then engine died. Turned off a/c and it is fine unless I turn it on.||||reg||1
Z||000001||EdsB52||08-07-2000||06:55 PM||||Definitely, change the accumulator, orifice tube (if it has one), and all O-rings. If the compressor shelled, it may have sent debris to the accumulator. Is $30 worth a $300 compressor? I just changed the whole A/C system out in my 89 Ford P/u, and I went with a Pep Boys special. Seems to work fine, but time hasn't tested it yet. I asked the same questions about factory new vs. rebuilt. Kind of a crap-shoot.<P>Oh, and check the manifold line to and from the compressor. If it's bad, you can have one re-fabed from the old ends for about $60.||||reg||1
Z||000002||theogre||08-08-2000||03:51 PM||||The compressor warrantee usually requires you to change the ACC/Dryer and orifice. That should give you an idea.<P>New vs rebuilt.... always a good question. Never a good easy answer.||||reg||1
Z||000003||DaveL||08-10-2000||09:48 AM||||Well, I went and bought a reman compressor. Had it for a day and decided to take it back and get the new AC/Delco comp. and accumulator. Not only does the Delco unit look better, it had several different packs of O-rings and seals included with it. Will get it installed next week and let ya know what happens. Living in Florida has its disadvantages, like heat, temps over 100 with humidity the same, old folk road hazards, and not enough Fieros (at least where I live).||||reg||12
